#!/usr/bin/env xetal
# HEX1000 as a calculator: each line types a key sequence from reset at
# the machine running its ROM program (rom/calc.asm) and shows the
# eight-digit screen it ends with, then how many instructions it took
# (a board runs 13.5 million a second). The screens are the Radix
# library's, key for key (just demo-lib Radix session; tests/calc.xtl
# checks 33 sequences). Run with "just demo-lib Hex1000 calc".
"hx:" u_se< "Hex1000"
hx:c_alc "12+34="
hx:c_alc "FF+1="
hx:c_alc "A*B="
hx:c_alc "C0DE+BEEF="
hx:c_alc "5-7="
hx:c_alc "FFFFFFFF+1="
hx:c_alc "2*3+4="
hx:c_alc "FFFFFFFF*FFFFFFFF="
hx:c_ost "12+34="
hx:c_ost "FFFFFFFF*FFFFFFFF="
